{
  "slug": "descriptive-predicate",
  "title": "Descriptive Predicate",
  "definition": "A [term:predicate] that attributes a property or quality to a referent — also called a predicative adjective construction. The predicate head is an adjective (or adjective-like word) rather than a noun. Descriptive predicates are crosslinguistically distinct from [term:classification-predicate]s: some languages use different [term:copula]s (Spanish ser vs. estar), different morphology, or different word-class assignments for the two functions. In some languages adjectives pattern like verbs and head predicates directly; in others they require a copula.",
  "relatedTerms": ["classification-predicate", "copula", "verbless-clause", "predicate", "word-class"],
  "examples": [
